Golden cases: Appendix C of the design (rows 1-148, E1-E18) plus synthetic
ov-<id> rows naming every overlay rule that no Appendix C row exercises.
Rows whose expectation is "unchanged" under both policies with the zero
Config are in negative.txt instead.

Each "-- <id> --" section is one case: "key: value" lines, value = rest of the
line verbatim; blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.

  in:          input URL (required, once)
  want:        expected Clean output under AffiliateKeep, and under
               AffiliateStrip unless want-strip is given; "unchanged" = input
  want-strip:  expected Clean output under AffiliateStrip
  policy:      both (default), keep or strip; with strip only, want: is the
               AffiliateStrip expectation
  config:      JSON object decoded into linkclean.Config (no Affiliate, no Sources)
  rules:       space-separated full IDs of the overlay rules the case exercises
               (each changes the result when disabled)
  abandoned:   true => Result.UnwrapAbandoned
  skipped:     expected Result.Skipped (scheme, unparseable, ambiguous,
               toolong, archive, roundcap)
  hops: none | hop: <JSON>       one per hop, in order; listed fields compared
  removed: none | removed: <JSON> one per Removal, in Removed order; listed
               fields compared, count must equal len(Removed)
  kept: <JSON> one per Kept entry ({"name","reason"}); count compared
  note:        free text (Appendix C note; marks: † changed in v2, ‡ amendment,
               ◆ maintainer amendment, § depends on a capture-status entry)

Every case also asserts Clean(out) == out, Explain(in).URL == Clean(in), and,
when out != in, no byte <= 0x20 or 0x7F in out and url.Parse(out) succeeds.
-- 1 --
note: basic
in: https://example.com/?utm_source=x&id=7
want: https://example.com/?id=7
